<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aldgisl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 678</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aldgisl was a king of the Frisians in the late 7th century, the first whose name is reliably known. In 678–679 he gave shelter to the English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfrid">Wilfrid</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>, who preached to the Frisians on his way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and he reportedly refused a Frankish demand to hand Wilfrid over. He was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redbad">Redbad</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aldgisl.jpg" alt="Aldgisl" width="320" height="611" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aldgillis2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
